MFA_CLEAR_NOTICE.text:
Someone asked for two-step sign-in to be turned off on the Glazecalc account {account}, because every authenticator app, passkey and recovery code for it was lost.

Two-step sign-in will be turned off on {date} unless you write to privacy@glazecalcapp.com before then. After that, the account can be signed in to with its password alone.

If this was you, there is nothing else to do. If not, write to privacy@glazecalcapp.com now, and reset your password right away at {forgot}

-- 
Glazecalc, {app}

MFA_OFF.text:
Two-step sign-in was just turned off on the Glazecalc account {account}: every authenticator app, passkey and recovery code was removed, and every device that was signed in has been signed out. Signing in now needs only the password.

You can turn two-step sign-in on again on your account page. If you did not ask for this, reset your password right away at {forgot}

-- 
Glazecalc, {app}

MFA_REMOVED.text:
This was just removed from the Glazecalc account {account} as a second step for signing in: {method}. If it was the last one, signing in now needs only the password.

If this was you, there is nothing else to do. If not, reset your password right away at {forgot}

