Glazecalc, {app}

SECOND_STEP_UNFINISHED.text:
Someone entered the right password for the Glazecalc account {account}, but did not finish the second step of signing in. Your second step kept them out.

If this was you, there is nothing else to do. If not, someone knows your password: change it right away. You can reset it at {forgot}

After 10 wrong codes from an authenticator app, codes are refused for an hour; after 10 more, for a day; and then for a week each time. A passkey or a recovery code still works while codes are refused. Resetting your password by email shuts that person out: any sign-in they started ends, the password they know stops working, and codes work again.

-- 
Glazecalc, {app}

